<Slide style={{ width: 1280, height: 720, background: '#FFFFFF', padding: '60px', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
  <Box style={{ height: 64, background: '#1E4FA8', flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'center', justifyContent: 'space-between', paddingLeft: 24, paddingRight: 24 }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 32, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#FFFFFF' }}>What this project establishes</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 16, color: '#FFFFFF', opacity: 0.8 }}>10 · Conclusion</Text>
  </Box>

  <Box style={{ marginTop: 26, flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'flex-start', gap: 20, paddingBottom: 16, borderBottom: '1px solid #D6DCE5' }}>
    <Text style={{ width: 60, fontSize: 34, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#1E4FA8', lineHeight: 1.1 }}>01</Text>
    <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 6 }}>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 22, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.3 }}>Five groups, and that number is argued, not assumed</Text>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#4A5568', lineHeight: 1.5 }}>Silhouette 0.555 at k = 5, stable under bootstrapping (ARI 0.979) and reproduced by Ward clustering and a Gaussian mixture. DBSCAN's failure is explained, not hidden.</Text>
    </Box>
  </Box>

  <Box style={{ marginTop: 16, flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'flex-start', gap: 20, paddingBottom: 16, borderBottom: '1px solid #D6DCE5' }}>
    <Text style={{ width: 60, fontSize: 34, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#1E4FA8', lineHeight: 1.1 }}>02</Text>
    <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 6 }}>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 22, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.3 }}>Income alone would merge the best and the worst customers</Text>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#4A5568', lineHeight: 1.5 }}>C3 and C4 both earn about 87k$ and differ by 65 spending points. Adding age as a third dimension lowers the silhouette from 0.555 to 0.417 — a descriptor, not a clustering axis.</Text>
    </Box>
  </Box>

  <Box style={{ marginTop: 16, flexDirection: 'row', alignItems: 'flex-start', gap: 20 }}>
    <Text style={{ width: 60, fontSize: 34, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#1E4FA8', lineHeight: 1.1 }}>03</Text>
    <Box style={{ flex: 1, flexDirection: 'column', gap: 6 }}>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 22, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#1A2230', lineHeight: 1.3 }}>The classifier is a convenience, not a discovery</Text>
      <Text style={{ fontSize: 18, color: '#4A5568', lineHeight: 1.5 }}>97.5% cross-validated accuracy reproduces the K-Means rule from four fields; 40.0% from demographics alone marks the limit of what a customer profile predicts.</Text>
    </Box>
  </Box>

  <Box style={{ marginTop: 20, background: '#F7F9FC', border: '1px solid #D6DCE5', padding: '14px 20px', flexDirection: 'column', gap: 6 }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 15, fontWeight: 'bold', color: '#1E4FA8', letterSpacing: 1 }}>LIMITATIONS</Text>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 17, color: '#4A5568', lineHeight: 1.45 }}>200 records limit inference on the smallest segment; the spending score is an opaque proxy, not revenue; the design is cross-sectional, with no recency or frequency; and k = 6 remains defensible — it would split the affluent Target segment.</Text>
  </Box>


  <Box style={{ position: 'absolute', top: 686, left: 0, width: 1160, flexDirection: 'row', justifyContent: 'flex-end' }}>
    <Text style={{ fontSize: 13, color: '#8B97A8' }}>10 / 12</Text>
  </Box>
</Slide>
